# Applies the repository-scoped settings to every ./mvnw invocation, so a corporate
# mirror in ~/.m2/settings.xml cannot silently become this project every build. See
# .mvn/settings.xml for the reasoning.
#
# Each line is one argument, which is why the flag and its value are on separate lines:
# "-s .mvn/settings.xml" on one line is passed as a single argument and Maven looks for a
# file whose name begins with a space.
-s
.mvn/settings.xml
